Hi [~accountid:5da9d068fb31ca0c35bfdd56] , please find below my comments to the agreement:

# Article 2.2 - _dates specified in the SOW are estimates only and time will not be of the essence for the performance of the Services_ - such provision generates a risk of each phase of the Services being delayed (e.g. Phase 1 may take 20, instead of 6-8 weeks indicated in SOW). If time is an important part of the Services, please consider removing this part of this article;
# Article 4.1 - _Where any advance payment of fees, costs or expenses is agreed in the SOW any such payment will be made immediately upon receipt of an invoice -_ For the avoidance of doubt I suggest adding “, no later than 7 days from receiving of such invoice”
# Article 5.4 - _This Article 5 shall survive termination or expiry of this Agreement for a period of two years_ - I suggest changing the period to 5 years (or at least 3);
# Article 9.1 _The Services Provider may, without disclosing the Client’s identity_ -_if requested_-_, ask a third party or agent to carry out or act in relation to some of the Services to obtain information of any kind and in any form whatsoever (and howsoever recorded, reproduced, transmitted or sorted)._ - I would remove “if requested”. Our identity should not be disclosed.
# Article 11.6 _No claim shall be brought by the Client under or in connection with this Agreement after the expiry of one year from completion of the Services to which the claim relates._ - I would delete the whole provision or extend the period for brining a claim for at least 3 years.

