hey Johannes. 

{quote}The system shouldn’t allow that many refunds without any consequences to the driver{quote}

you’re absolutely right. we have the same concern. we raised this topic with the CS Automation team about a month ago. there are drivers with thousands of euros in refunds with bolt at fault in a couple of months only. overcharge schemes nowadays are even more profitable than they were before. when a driver overcharges customers, not everyone complains to CS, so depending on the country, they can get away with profit. but now with AI refunds not even touching the driver money, these schemes are much more profitable. 

when we raised this topic to CS Product, to mitigate, they adjusted the actor at fault for a couple of issue_keys. refunds for ride didn’t happen and cancellation fees are back to deduct from the driver’s balance. the proper solution will come from driverX. verticals are taking ownership of actor at fault decision. eventually, driverX will decide for each refund to take it from driver’s balance or not. 

