Hi all - just adding my comments from slack, which is just background for the purposes of the UK specific review. 

----

{color:#0747a6}*Background / Considerations:*{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Setting some low-impact rules to prevent price recalculations is clearly necessary to curb the impact of geolocation errors (+ similar glitches) and irritating passengers. At the extreme end of the spectrum, there is scope for drivers to exploit and facilitate an overcharge.{color}

* {color:#0747a6}However, drivers may take any ‘reasonable route’ and Bolt does not require drivers to follow a certain route. Rules that 'avoid recalculating prices' therefore ought to cover data glitches and routes taken that are are (probably...) ‘not reasonable’.{color}

* {color:#0747a6}It’s not uncommon for drivers with local knowledge to choose routes based on local traffic factors (time of day etc.), which as far as I know are not currently taken into account by our own in-app directions. This may explain why alternative routes are taken. All things considered, we shouldn’t assume that drivers are deliberately ‘nickel and dimming’ passengers by taking alternative routes, unless we have data that backs this up.{color}

* {color:#0747a6}It’s also worth remembering that prices presented to passengers are ‘estimates’ and are ‘subject to change’. There is not a promise to any passenger in any market that prices will not increase if appropriate.{color}

{color:#0747a6}*Putting that into practical action points:*{color}

* {color:#0747a6}All “relevant %s” that apply for limiting recalculations should properly balance the interests of Bolt, customers AND drivers - if we are not confident that the current %s strike the right balance, then they ought to be reviewed.{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Severe controls may escalate driver complaints + used to evidence that drivers tare subject to extreme 'over control'. To reduce the risk of this, controls ideally ought to be aimed at avoiding ‘unreasonable / incorrect pricing’ (rather than to always prioritise the customer experience {color}{color:#0747a6}_over_{color}{color:#0747a6} the driver experience).{color}

{color:#0747a6}*Quick reminder of UK specific info:*{color}{color:#0747a6}The sensitivity of setting ‘price recalculations’ is ultimately the same in all markets - all drivers rightly expect Bolt to ‘payout properly’ based on time/duration - but here’s a quick reminder of quirks of the ‘UK principal model’:{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Bolt itself is the service provider and is setting the passenger prices {color}{color:#0747a6}_for itself_ {color}{color:#0747a6}(rather than {color}{color:#0747a6}_on behalf of drivers_{color}{color:#0747a6}).{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Bolt pays the driver out of our own pocket (rather than passing drivers their own earnings which we have simply collected {color}{color:#0747a6}_on their behalf_{color}{color:#0747a6}).{color}

{color:#0747a6}_(exception = drivers on the ‘true taxi’ UK categories which remain on Bolt’s standard ‘agency model’)_{color}

